#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:30
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "&kde;, is used on a wide variety of computers by a wide variety of users. Under the category of performance, this dialog allows each user to adjust options which may make the computer that &konqueror; is installed on feel more responsive."
msgid "&konqueror;, is used on a wide variety of computers by a wide variety of users. Under the category of performance, this dialog allows each user to adjust options which may make the computer that &konqueror; is installed on feel more responsive."
msgstr "&kde; úsase en moi diversos computadores por usuarios moi diferentes. Na categoría de rendemento agrúpanse os parámetros que cada usuario pode axustar para facer que o computador no que está instalado o &konqueror; responda máis á presa."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preloading"
msgstr "Precarga"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:35
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "The subsection labeled <guilabel>Preloading</guilabel> also makes a tradeoff between memory and performance."
msgid "The subsection labeled <guilabel>Preloading</guilabel> makes a tradeoff between memory and performance."
msgstr "A subsección chamada <guilabel>Precarga</guilabel> tamén fai un balance entre memoria e rendemento."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:37
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "<emphasis>Preloading</emphasis> refers to loading an instance of &konqueror; into memory before a user asks to start &konqueror;. The positive effect of this is that when a user asks &kde; to load &konqueror; the window appears instantly because most of the application has been preloaded. The negative effect is that this instance of &konqueror; uses memory that could be used by other programs. By default, when a user closes &konqueror;, &kde; does not close the instance. This means that the next time a user wants &konqueror; loaded, it is nearly instantaneous again."
msgid "<emphasis>Preloading</emphasis> refers to loading an instance of &konqueror; into memory before a user asks to start &konqueror;. The positive effect of this is that when a user asks to load &konqueror; the window appears instantly because most of the application has been preloaded. The negative effect is that this instance of &konqueror; uses memory that could be used by other programs. By default, when a user closes &konqueror;, the instance is not closed. This means that the next time a user wants &konqueror; loaded, it is nearly instantaneous again."
msgstr "<emphasis>Precargar</emphasis> refírese a cargar unha instancia do &konqueror; na memoria antes de que o usuario inicie o programa. O efecto positivo disto é que cando o usuario lle pida a &kde; que cargue o &konqueror; a xanela hase amosar instantaneamente porque a maior parte do programa xa estará cargado. O efecto negativo é que esta instancia do &konqueror; usa memoria que poderían usar outros programas. Por omisión, cando un usuario pecha o &konqueror;, &kde; non pecha a instancia, deste xeito a vindeira vez que o usuario cargue o &konqueror; abrirase ao momento."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:42
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "The final check box labeled <guilabel>Always try to have at least one preloaded instance</guilabel> signals to &kde; that you always want &kde; to have one preloaded, but not used, instance of &konqueror; available. This option will actually decrease performance on some machines (especially those with limited physical memory)."
msgid "The final check box labeled <guilabel>Always try to have at least one preloaded instance</guilabel> signals that you always want to have one preloaded, but not used, instance of &konqueror; available. This option will actually decrease performance on some machines (especially those with limited physical memory)."
msgstr "A opción etiquetada como <guilabel>Tentar sempre ter polo menos unha sesión precargada</guilabel> indícalle a &kde; que debe procurar ter unha sesión do &konqueror; precargada pero non usaada. Nalgunhas máquinas esta opcións reducirá o rendemento (especialmente nas que teñan pouca memoria)."
